uides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"Cost Formula"},"644":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"Example (n=1024)"},"645":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-19","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"`fft`, `ifft`"},"646":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-20","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"$5n \\cdot \\lceil\\log_2 n\\rceil$"},"647":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-21","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"51,200"},"648":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-22","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"`rfft`, `irfft`"},"649":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-23","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"$5(n/2) \\cdot \\lceil\\log_2 n\\rceil$"},"650":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-24","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"25,600"},"651":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-25","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"`fft2`, `ifft2`"},"652":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-26","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"$5N \\cdot \\lceil\\log_2 N\\rceil$ where $N = n_\\{1\\} \\cdot n_\\{2\\}$"},"653":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-27","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"varies"},"654":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-28","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"`fftn`, `ifftn`"},"655":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-29","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"$5N \\cdot \\lceil\\log_2 N\\rceil$ where $N = \\prod_\\{i\\} n_\\{i\\}$"},"656":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-30","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"varies"},"657":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-31","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"`fftfreq`, `rfftfreq`"},"658":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-32","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"0 (free)"},"659":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-33","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"0"},"660":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-34","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"`fftshift`, `ifftshift`"},"661":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-35","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"0 (free)"},"662":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-36","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"0"},"663":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-37","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#cost-model","content":"Real-valued transforms (`rfft`, `irfft`, `rfftn`, `irfftn`) cost roughly half of their complex counterparts because they exploit conjugate symmetry."},"664":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-38","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#real-vs-complex-transforms","content":"When your input is real-valued (which is common in signal processing), prefer `rfft` over `fft` — it costs half as much:"},"665":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-39","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#real-vs-complex-transforms","content":"The output of `rfft` has shape `(n//2 + 1,)` instead of `(n,)`, since the negative frequencies are redundant for real inputs."},"666":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-40","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#multi-dimensional-fft","content":"Use `fft2` for 2-D transforms (e.g., images) and `fftn` for arbitrary dimensions:"},"667":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-41","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#windowed-fft-pattern","content":"A common signal processing pattern — window the signal before FFT to reduce spectral leakage:"},"668":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-42","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#common-pitfalls","content":"**Symptom:** Using `fnp.fft.fft` on real data when `fnp.fft.rfft` would suffice"},"669":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-43","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#common-pitfalls","content":"**Fix:** `rfft` costs half as much. If your input is real-valued, always prefer `rfft`/`irfft` over `fft`/`ifft`."},"670":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-44","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#common-pitfalls","content":"**Symptom:** Unexpectedly high cost for multi-dimensional FFT"},"671":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-45","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#common-pitfalls","content":"**Fix:** The cost scales as $5 \\cdot \\prod n_\\{i\\} \\cdot \\lceil\\log_2(\\prod n_\\{i\\})\\rceil$. A 256x256 2-D FFT processes 65,536 elements, not 256. Use `fft_cost` to estimate before running."},"672":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-46","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#related-pages","content":"API Reference — full function signatures and docstrings"},"673":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-47","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#related-pages","content":"Plan Your Budget — general cost estimation workflow"},"674":{"id":"/docs/guides/fft-48","page_id":"/docs/guides/fft","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/fft#related-pages","content":"FLOP Counting Model — how all costs are computed"},"675":{"id":"/docs/g