age_id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/infrastructure/docker#time-limit-enforcement","content":"**Container-level (hard):** The Docker container enforces a kernel-level time limit via cgroups/rlimit. If the in-library check doesn't catch the overshoot (e.g., a single very long numpy call), the container delivers `SIGKILL`. This is the ultimate backstop — no Python code can escape it."},"1201":{"id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker-31","page_id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/infrastructure/docker#time-limit-enforcement","content":"Signal-based preemption (`SIGALRM`) is deliberately not used because Python signal handlers cannot interrupt C extensions (numpy/LAPACK/BLAS), making them ineffective for exactly the operations where time limits matter most."},"1202":{"id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker-32","page_id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/infrastructure/docker#common-pitfalls","content":"**Symptom:** `Connection refused` or `timeout`"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker-33","page_id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/infrastructure/docker#common-pitfalls","content":"**Fix:** Ensure the server is running before starting the client. Check that `FLOPSCOPE_SERVER_URL` matches the server's `--url` argument."},"1204":{"id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker-34","page_id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/infrastructure/docker#common-pitfalls","content":"**Symptom:** Port conflict"},"1205":{"id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker-35","page_id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/infrastructure/docker#common-pitfalls","content":"**Fix:** Change the port in both the server `--url` and client `FLOPSCOPE_SERVER_URL`."},"1206":{"id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker-36","page_id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/infrastructure/docker#related-pages","content":"Client-Server Model — architecture overview"},"1207":{"id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker-37","page_id":"/docs/infrastructure/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/infrastructure/docker#related-pages","content":"Contributor Guide — local repo workflows"},"1208":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","type":"page","content":"FLOP Counting Model","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Understanding Flopscope"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model"},"1209":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-0","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","content":"How Flopscope bills compute: the cost model, by family rule."},"1210":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#cost-model-reference","content":"Cost model reference"},"1211":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-2","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#how-to-read-this","content":"How to read this"},"1212":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-3","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#billing-model--design-principles","content":"Billing model & design principles"},"1213":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-4","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#fma2","content":"FMA=2"},"1214":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-5","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#comparison-and-select","content":"Comparison and select"},"1215":{"id":"/docs/understan