dule-level-generator-randomstate","content":"`numel(output)`"},"2039":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-830","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"16.0"},"2040":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-831","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"DECLARED"},"2041":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-832","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"`_cost_formulas.py`"},"2042":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-833","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"`Generator.multivariate_hypergeometric` (`method='count'`)"},"2043":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-834","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"`sum(colors) + 2 × num_variates × min(nsample, sum(colors) − nsample) + numel(output)`"},"2044":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-835","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"16.0"},"2045":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-836","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"DERIVED composite: numpy builds a temporary counting buffer of length `sum(colors)`, then for each of the `num_variates` output draws does a partial Fisher-Yates shuffle over `min(nsample, sum(colors) − nsample)` buffer entries (whichever of the sampled/excluded side is smaller), followed by a separate pass counting the colors of those same shuffled entries — two full passes over that length"},"2046":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-837","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"`_cost_formulas.py`"},"2047":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-838","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"`random.beta`, `random.dirichlet`, `random.f`, `random.gamma`, `random.gumbel`, `random.laplace`, `random.logistic`, `random.lognormal`, `random.logseries`, `random.pareto`, `random.power`, `random.rayleigh`, `random.standard_cauchy`, `random.standard_exponential`, `random.standard_gamma`, `random.standard_t`, `random.triangular`, `random.vonmises`, `random.wald`, `random.weibull`, `random.zipf`"},"2048":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-839","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"`numel(output)`"},"2049":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-840","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"16.0"},"2050":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-841","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"DECLARED: flop\\_cost = numel(output); transcendental weight 16.0 for all continuous/transformed distributions; each draw resolves to its actual output dtype — float64 (rate 2.0) for the continuous members, int64 (rate 2.0) for the discrete `logseries`/`zipf` — so the full bill is `32 × numel` in practice"},"2051":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-842","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"`_cost_formulas.py`"},"2052":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-843","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"**Complex dtypes**: the distribution samplers produce **real-only** outputs, so a complex\nresolved dtype is `complex_factor = \"illegal\"` and raises. A draw bills at its **output\ndtype's** rate — `standard_normal(dtype=float64)` bills `2×` the float32 draw. The\ndata-movement random ops (`shuffle`, `permutation`, `choice`, `Generator.permuted`) permute\ncaller-supplied values of any dtype and are billed dtype-neutrally — their cost counts\nthe selection work, which is width-independent — so complex input does not raise."},"2053":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-844","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#random-module-level-generator-randomstate","content":"Source: `src/flopscope/numpy/random/_cost_formulas.py`."},"2054":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-845","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#stats","content":"Stats ops are composite (weight 1.0; all per-element factors in `flop_cost`).\nThe billed element count is the numel of the broadcast of the input with the\ndistribution parameters — array-valued `loc`/`scale` (or `a`/`b`/`s`) enlarge\nthe output beyond `x` and are charged accordingly. Every `stats.*` kernel computes\nin float64 regardless of the input's own dtype, so the real bill is `2×` the\nper-element counts below even for a float32 input (e.g. `stats.uniform.pdf` on a\n10-element float32 array bills `20`, not `10`)."},"2055":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-846","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#stats","content":"Op"},"2056":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-847","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#stats","content":"flop\\_cost (per element)"},"2057":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-848","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#stats","content":"basis"},"2058":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-849","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#stats","content":"`stats.norm.pdf`"},"2059":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-850","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#stats","content":"27"},"2060":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-851","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#stats","content":"DERIVED: exp(17) + affine normalization(10); composite, weight 1.0"},"2061":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-852","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#stats","content":"`stats.norm.cdf`"},"2062":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-853","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/unde