n writing a single given input through unchanged."},"2336":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1127","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"**Selector-deriving ops are charged** (they *test* values to produce the selector,\nunlike the ops above whose selector is a given input):"},"2337":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1128","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"Op"},"2338":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1129","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"flop\\_cost"},"2339":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1130","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"basis"},"2340":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1131","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"`nonzero`, `where(cond)` (1-arg)"},"2341":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1132","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"`numel(input)` (weight 1.0)"},"2342":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1133","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"DECLARED: implicit `!= 0` scan per element"},"2343":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1134","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-g