se they perform per-bit/index work or I/O beyond pure relocation:"},"2390":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1181","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"Op"},"2391":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1182","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"flop\\_cost"},"2392":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1183","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"basis"},"2393":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1184","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"source"},"2394":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1185","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"`copyto`"},"2395":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1186","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"`numel(dst)` (or popcount(`where`) when masked)"},"2396":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1187","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather-ops-with-distinct-charged-siblings","content":"DECLARED: priced per element written, unconditionally — same-dtype or not (see §Boundary ops)"},"2397":{"id":"/do