on-categories-55","page_id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories#reduction-cost-surfaces","content":"flopscope splits reductions into two cost surfaces:"},"2672":{"id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories-56","page_id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories#reduction-cost-surfaces","content":"**Tier 1 — additive accumulation** (`sum`, `prod`, `max`, `min`, `all`, `any`, bitwise/logical `or`/`and`/`xor`, `mean`).\nCharges `(unique input entries − unique output cells) + extra ops`. `mean` adds one divide per unique output cell."},"2673":{"id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories-57","page_id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories#reduction-cost-surfaces","content":"**Tier 2 — selection-style reductions** (`median`, `percentile`, `quantile`).\nCharges `(unique output cells) × (per-output cost)`. Each output cell needs a full partition pass over the reduced axes; symmetry helps when output cells share an orbit."},"2674":{"id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories-58","page_id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories#reduction-cost-surfaces","content":"See Symmetry-aware FLOP counting for the mental model and worked examples."},"2675":{"id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories-59","page_id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories#blacklisted-operations","content":"Operations not relevant to numerical computation. Calling them raises an `AttributeError`. These are I/O, configuration, datetime, and display functions that have no meaningful FLOP cost."},"2676":{"id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories-60","page_id":"/docs/understanding/operation-categories","tags":[],"type":"